# Cleaning Schedule Agent — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your own values.
# Never commit your real `.env` to git.
#
# The skill itself does not read this file. Its configuration
# (tool paths, sheet ID, property ID, room count) goes into the
# placeholder values in .claude/skills/cleaning-schedule/SKILL.md
# — see "Customising" in the README.
#
# This file is for the secrets that YOUR OWN tools need: the PMS
# wrapper scripts and the email + sheets CLI that the skill calls.
# Use whatever variable names those tools expect. The lines below
# are examples; delete the ones you do not need.

# ============================================================
# PMS (Property Management System) credentials
# ============================================================
# Example for a Cloudbeds-based wrapper. Any PMS with reservation
# list, reservation detail and reservation-notes endpoints works.

# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_ID=""
# CLOUDBEDS_CLIENT_SECRET=""
# CLOUDBEDS_ACCESS_TOKEN=""
# CLOUDBEDS_REFRESH_TOKEN=""

# ============================================================
# Email + sheets CLI
# ============================================================
# Most Google Workspace CLIs keep their login in their own config
# folder and need nothing here. Add a variable only if yours
# reads one from the environment.
